Rem ==================================================================
Rem turtle.shoddy — Shoddy standard library: turtle graphics.
Rem
Rem A thin, purely functional turtle over the scribbler. LOGO's turtle is
Rem the canonical mutable object; Shoddy has no mutation, so the turtle is
Rem a VALUE threaded through the program exactly as the scribbler handle
Rem is: every command takes a Turtle and returns a new one, drawing into
Rem the shared pixel buffer as a side effect. LOGO's control half (REPEAT,
Rem TO..END, IF) is not reimplemented — Shoddy already is that language:
Rem   REPEAT 4 [FD 50 RT 90]  ==  Fold(Range(1,4), t, Fn(t,_) => TurnRight(Forward(t,50),90))
Rem
Rem Heading is in DEGREES, 0 = up (north), increasing CLOCKWISE — the
Rem turtle convention. The scribbler's y grows downward, so the unit step
Rem for heading h is (sin h, -cos h): h=0 up, h=90 east, h=180 down.
Rem
Rem Position is kept FRACTIONAL and rounded only when handing endpoints to
Rem DrawLine. Snapping the pose to integers would compound error over many
Rem small steps and a polygon would not close.
Rem
Rem The turn words are TurnLeft/TurnRight, not Left/Right: Left and Right
Rem are the string builtins (Left$/Right$), and a Def silently shadows a
Rem builtin. Windowed program (mill run) like every scribbler program.
Rem ==================================================================

Include "scribbler.shoddy"
Include "math.shoddy"

Type Turtle
    Sc      As Scribbler   Rem the drawing surface (mutated in place)
    X       As Number      Rem fractional pen position
    Y       As Number
    Heading As Number      Rem degrees, 0 = up, clockwise positive
    Pen     As Boolean     Rem down = drawing
    R       As Number
    G       As Number
    B       As Number

Rem ---- construction & lifecycle --------------------------------------

Rem Open a surface, park the turtle at its centre facing up, pen down,
Rem drawing in white on black.
Def NewTurtle(width As Number, height As Number) As Turtle
    Let sc = ScribblerFill(ScribblerOpen(width, height), 0, 0, 0)
    Turtle(sc, width / 2, height / 2, 0, True, 255, 255, 255)

Rem Recentre on the surface facing up; pen and colour are kept.
Def Home(t As Turtle) As Turtle
    Turtle(Sc(t), ScribblerWidth(Sc(t)) / 2, ScribblerHeight(Sc(t)) / 2, 0, Pen(t), R(t), G(t), B(t))

Rem Present the buffer. The drawing already happened in place, so the
Rem turtle is unchanged — Blit only pushes pixels to the window.
Def Blit(t As Turtle) As Turtle
    Let shown = ScribblerBlit(Sc(t))
    t

Def Close(t As Turtle) As Turtle
    Let closed = ScribblerClose(Sc(t))
    t

Def Title(t As Turtle, s As String) As Turtle
    Let named = ScribblerTitle(Sc(t), s)
    t

Rem ---- motion --------------------------------------------------------

Rem The shared core: move to (nx, ny), drawing the segment from the
Rem current position first iff the pen is down, and carry the heading.
Def MoveTo(t As Turtle, nx As Number, ny As Number) As Turtle
    Let sc2 = PenSegment(t, nx, ny)
    Turtle(sc2, nx, ny, Heading(t), Pen(t), R(t), G(t), B(t))

Def PenSegment(t As Turtle, nx As Number, ny As Number) As Scribbler
    If Pen(t) Then
        DrawLine(Sc(t), Round(X(t)), Round(Y(t)), Round(nx), Round(ny), R(t), G(t), B(t))
    Else
        Sc(t)

Def Forward(t As Turtle, d As Number) As Turtle
    Let rad = Rad(Heading(t))
    MoveTo(t, X(t) + d * Sin(rad), Y(t) - d * Cos(rad))

Def Back(t As Turtle, d As Number) As Turtle
    Forward(t, -d)

Rem Jump/draw to an absolute point — respects the pen, exactly like Forward.
Def SetXY(t As Turtle, x As Number, y As Number) As Turtle
    MoveTo(t, x, y)

Rem ---- turning -------------------------------------------------------

Def SetHeading(t As Turtle, deg As Number) As Turtle
    Turtle(Sc(t), X(t), Y(t), Wrap(deg, 360), Pen(t), R(t), G(t), B(t))

Def TurnRight(t As Turtle, deg As Number) As Turtle
    SetHeading(t, Heading(t) + deg)

Def TurnLeft(t As Turtle, deg As Number) As Turtle
    SetHeading(t, Heading(t) - deg)

Rem Face an absolute point. In screen coords (y down) with heading 0 = up,
Rem the heading toward (px, py) is atan2(dx, -dy). The target params are
Rem px/py, not x/y: a param named x folds to X and would shadow the X
Rem accessor, so X(t) would read the parameter instead of the field.
Def SetTowards(t As Turtle, px As Number, py As Number) As Turtle
    SetHeading(t, Deg(Atn2(px - X(t), Y(t) - py)))

Def DistanceTo(t As Turtle, px As Number, py As Number) As Number
    Dist(X(t), Y(t), px, py)

Rem ---- pen -----------------------------------------------------------

Def PenUp(t As Turtle) As Turtle
    Turtle(Sc(t), X(t), Y(t), Heading(t), False, R(t), G(t), B(t))

Def PenDown(t As Turtle) As Turtle
    Turtle(Sc(t), X(t), Y(t), Heading(t), True, R(t), G(t), B(t))

Def SetPenColor(t As Turtle, r As Number, g As Number, b As Number) As Turtle
    Turtle(Sc(t), X(t), Y(t), Heading(t), Pen(t), r, g, b)
